# Copy this file to .env.local (on your computer) and/or add the variables in Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables.
#
# The address of the realtime server (see README, "Make it truly realtime").
# Leave it empty to keep the plain version that works on Vercel alone.
#   locally on the same computer:      http://localhost:4000
#   on your network (friends' phones): http://YOUR-COMPUTER-IP:4000
#   online (Render, Railway, Fly...):  https://your-realtime-server.onrender.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=

# On the REALTIME SERVER (Render...) - not needed in Vercel if you only use the plain version:
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN  (or KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN)
#       Keeps player profiles, stats and the leaderboard for good (a free Upstash database is enough).
#       Without it they are kept in memory: a device that comes back gives its profile back to the
#       server, but the leaderboard starts over when the server restarts.
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-game.vercel.app   (optional: only your website may connect)
#   PROFILES_FILE=./profiles.json                  (optional, your own computer: keep profiles in a file)
